---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactBanner from '../components/ContactBanner.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Services — Raashid Arquil" description="Business websites, focused web application features, and mobile prototypes. Discuss a bounded freelance project."><div class="shell">
<header class="page-intro compact-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Freelance services</p><h1 class="display">Let's build<br/><em class="serif">what you need.</em></h1><p class="lead">Start with a specific problem. We can define a useful piece of work, agree on the scope, and build from there.</p></header>
<section class="offer-list" aria-label="Services"><h2 class="sr-only">Services available</h2>
<article class="offer"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Websites</p><div><h3>A website for your business or product.</h3><p>Business websites, landing pages, and personal portfolios, using a coded implementation or WordPress and Elementor where appropriate.</p><ul><li>An agreed set of pages and responsive layouts.</li><li>Implementation from supplied content and a defined visual direction.</li><li>Deployment and handover included in the scope discussion.</li></ul><p class="offer-input">Bring: your offer, content, brand assets, and any reference sites. We can identify what is missing before starting.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact?topic=website">Discuss a website ↗</a></div></article>
<article class="offer"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Web applications</p><div><h3>One workflow, built properly.</h3><p>A dashboard, interface, or focused feature for an application. We start with who uses it and what they need to accomplish.</p><ul><li>A defined user flow and the screens it needs.</li><li>Agreed data connections and integration boundaries.</li><li>Review points to inspect the working result.</li></ul><p class="offer-input">Bring: the existing application or designs, the required behaviour, and access requirements.</p><a class="text-link" href="/work/smartdrive">Explore SmartDrive's prototype ↗</a></div></article>
<article class="offer"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Mobile prototypes</p><div><h3>A first version you can try.</h3><p>A bounded Android or Flutter prototype, interface implementation, or selected app feature.</p><ul><li>A specific user journey rather than an undefined whole app.</li><li>An implementation you can inspect and try.</li><li>Clear separation between prototype scope and release work.</li></ul><p class="offer-input">Bring: the intended users, essential flow, target devices, and any existing designs.</p><a class="text-link" href="/work/keepclose">Explore KeepClose ↗</a></div></article>
</section>
<section class="section"><p class="eyebrow mb-4">How we'll work</p><h2 class="section-title">Clear expectations<br/>at each step.</h2><div class="process-grid">{[{title:'Understand',text:'Discuss the problem, users, existing work, timing, and budget.'},{title:'Agree',text:'Define deliverables, milestones, review points, and responsibilities. Scope changes are discussed separately.'},{title:'Build & review',text:'Inspect progress at agreed milestones and keep decisions clear.'},{title:'Hand over',text:'Agree deployment, access, documentation, and any support before delivery.'}].map((step,i)=><article><span class="eyebrow">0{i+1}</span><h3>{step.title}</h3><p>{step.text}</p></article>)}</div><p class="small-copy mt-8">These describe how I intend to structure an engagement. Availability, costs, and support depend on the agreed project.</p></section><ContactBanner/>
</div></BaseLayout>
